[h1]🧟 Knox Survivors[/h1]

Knox Survivors adds human survivors to Project Zomboid, with the goal of making them feel like other people trying to survive in the same world as you.

The original idea was inspired by survivor mods such as Superb Survivors. Knox Survivors and its survivor framework have been built from the ground up by me, .exe.

The goal is to keep the experience as close to vanilla Zomboid as possible. Loaded survivors use native player-based characters and normal clothing, cosmetics, weapons, items, containers, animations, and game systems wherever possible.

Survivors can scavenge, equip themselves, manage basic needs, fight, meet and recruit others, form groups, work around bases, and die. They are AI-controlled survivors in Project Zomboid—not colony-game pawns.

[h1]🚧 Current State[/h1]

Knox Survivors is actively being developed. The current rebuild includes persistent survivors, autonomous survival behavior, recruitment, companion orders, groups, combat, scavenging, base work, and survivor management.

[b]Current development focus:[/b] Making companions more reliable during ordinary survival: following you, passing through doorways and fences, responding to danger, obeying orders, and resuming what they were doing after interruptions. Recent work also covers native injury recovery, entrance permissions, vehicle boarding, resident schedules, and clearer order and job feedback.

Interface improvements also cover vanilla isometric and Project Viewpoint's first-person and third-person views.

These systems are still being improved. Pathfinding, firearms, competing orders, base jobs, and long-running saves may be unreliable or incomplete. Autonomous driving and larger faction events remain experimental.

[b]Current focus:[/b] Single-player. Full multiplayer support is not ready.
[b]Current target:[/b] Project Zomboid Build 42.21.
[b]Compatibility note:[/b] Full in-game testing of the latest unified build is still pending. The target version is not a guarantee that every feature works.
[b]Save advice:[/b] Use a new disposable save for testing. Back up saves you care about. Compatibility with older Knox Survivors save data is not guaranteed.

[h2]▶️ Install and play[/h2]

[b]Runtime update:[/b] This build packages one Knox Survivors mod with a choice of runtime:

[list]
[*][b]ZombieBuddy 2.3.4[/b] — the preferred runtime for Project Viewpoint.
[*][b]KnoxBridge Runtime[/b] — an independent alternative that does not require ZombieBuddy or Project Viewpoint.
[/list]

[b]Choose ONE runtime. Never run ZombieBuddy and KnoxBridge together.[/b]

[b]Version notice:[/b] The public Workshop download and Required Items may still reflect the older KnoxBridge setup. Check Discord for the current download and matching installation instructions before changing runtimes.

[list]
[*]Install Knox Survivors and follow the setup instructions for the runtime supported by your downloaded version. Subscribing to a Workshop dependency marker alone does not install the Java runtime.
[*][b]KnoxBridge setup:[/b] Download the separate setup from [url=https://github.com/exe-create/KnoxBridge/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url].
[*][b]Windows x64:[/b] Run [b]KnoxBridgeSetup.exe[/b] and choose [b]1 — Install/Update[/b]. It uses Project Zomboid's bundled Java; no separate Java installation is needed.
[*][b]Linux/macOS:[/b] Extract the Bridge ZIP, close Steam, open a terminal in the extracted folder, and run [b]sh scripts/setup-unix.sh[/b]. Choose [b]1 — Install/Update[/b]. Python 3 is required. This setup path has not been live-tested.
[*]Enable Knox Survivors and the appropriate runtime mod, then launch normally through Steam. The retired Knox Launcher/legacy agent is unsupported.
[*]Review the Knox Survivors Java module through your runtime's approval screen. KnoxBridge calls this [b]Review Java Mods[/b]. New or changed JARs may require fresh approval. Follow the selected runtime's prompts, including a full restart when required.
[/list]

[b]ZombieBuddy approval:[/b] This update uses normal unsigned-mod approval. Knox Survivors should appear as [b](unsigned)[/b] in [b]ZombieBuddy Java Mod Approval[/b]. Select [b]Allow[/b] for Knox Survivors, confirm the dialog, and restart if requested. [b]Trust author[/b] is not needed. This avoids the Steam author-key lookup that could return HTTP 429 and block loading. Custom policies that reject unsigned mods still apply; this mod does not change your runtime settings. If approval still fails, check Discord for guidance rather than disabling verification.

[h2]🔒 Compatibility and safety[/h2]

Java modules run with the same permissions as Project Zomboid. These runtimes are not sandboxes, so only allow Java mods you trust.

Other Java mods do not become compatible automatically; their authors may need to add support for your chosen runtime.

[b]Project Viewpoint support:[/b] Camera-aware interface support is implemented for its first-person and third-person views, alongside vanilla isometric play. Integration is still being improved; gameplay, camera interaction, and save/load reliability need further in-game testing with matching mod and runtime versions.

[b]Coming soon:[/b] Official Knox Drugs support. This integration is planned and is not included as a supported feature in this update.

